  "worked_solution": "Since $u$ and $w$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that $u\\cdot w=0.$ Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(w+v)\\cdot (2u+3w) & =2(w\\cdot u)+2(v\\cdot u)+3(w\\cdot w)+3(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =0+2(v\\cdot u)+3(w\\cdot w)+3(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =2(v\\cdot u)+3(w\\cdot w)+3(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =2(-4\\cdot 5+(-2)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-3)+(-4)\\cdot 3) \\\\  & +3(1\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-5)+2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & +3(-4\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-5)+2\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2(-40)+3(34)+3(2) \\\\  & =-80+102+6 \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
